ve volume is which?","o":["The total air in the lungs","Air that can still be breathed in after a normal inspiration","Air in the lung after maximal expiration","Air that can still be breathed out after a normal expiration","Air moved with each quiet breath"],"e":["Wrong. TLC.","Wrong. IRV.","Wrong. RV.","Correct.","Wrong. VT."],"a":3,"p":"682","k":"Lung volumes and capacities"},{"s":"Which capacity includes residual volume?","o":["Inspiratory capacity","Inspiratory reserve volume","Total lung capacity","Vital capacity","Tidal volume"],"e":["Wrong. No RV.","Wrong. A volume.","Correct.","Wrong. No RV.","Wrong. A volume."],"a":2,"p":"682","k":"Lung volumes and capacities"},{"s":"Work of breathing is defined as which?","o":["The cardiac output to the lungs","The energy or oxygen used by respiratory muscles to produce ventilation","The pressure in the pleural space","The volume of air moved per minute","The oxygen carried by hemoglobin"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Minute ventilation.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"682","k":"Work of breathing"}]},{"t":"Ventilation, compliance and pulmonary circulation","q":[{"s":"A man has a tidal volume of 500 mL and a respiratory rate of 12/min. What is his minute ventilation?","o":["6 L/min","4.2 L/min","12 L/min","0.5 L/min","1.8 L/min"],"e":["Correct. 500 × 12.","Wrong. Alveolar ventilation.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"683","k":"Ventilation"},{"s":"A man has VT 500 mL, dead space 150 mL and RR 12/min. What is his alveolar ventilation?","o":["3.5 L/min","4.2 L/min","7.8 L/min","6 L/min","1.8 L/min"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct. (500 − 150) × 12.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Minute ventilation.","Wrong. Dead space ventilation."],"a":1,"p":"683","k":"Ventilation"},{"s":"Which breathing pattern gives the highest alveolar ventilation at the same minute ventilation?","o":["All patterns are equal","Slow, deep breaths","Rapid, shallow breaths","Breath-holding","Panting"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct. Less dead space fraction.","Wrong. More dead space.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"683","k":"Ventilation"},{"s":"What is the normal respiratory rate in adults?","o":["30–40 breaths/min","6–10 breaths/min","25–30 breaths/min","40–60 breaths/min","12–20 breaths/min"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Newborn.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"683","k":"Ventilation"},{"s":"Why does lung inflation follow a different pressure–volume curve than deflation?","o":["Airway resistance falls on expiration","Diaphragm fatigue","Surface tension forces must be overcome during inflation (hysteresis)","Blood flow changes","The chest wall stiffens on inspiration"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":2,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"At FRC, what is the intrapleural pressure?","o":["Negative","Equal to arterial pressure","Zero","Positive","Equal to alveolar pressure"],"e":["Correct. Prevents atelectasis.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Airway pressure is zero.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"At which lung volume is pulmonary vascular resistance lowest?","o":["Total lung capacity","Vital capacity","Residual volume","Maximal expiration","Functional residual capacity"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"Compliance is defined as which?","o":["Volume per minute","Change in volume per change in pressure","Change in pressure per change in flow","Change in pressure per change in volume","Change in flow per unit time"],"e":["Wrong. Ventilation.","Correct.","Wrong. Resistance.","Wrong. Elastance.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"Lung compliance is increased in which condition?","o":["Emphysema","Pneumonia","Pulmonary fibrosis","ARDS","Pulmonary edema"],"e":["Correct. Also older adults.","Wrong. Decreased.","Wrong. Decreased.","Wrong. Decreased.","Wrong. Decreased."],"a":0,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"How does surfactant affect compliance?","o":["Increases surface tension","Decreases it","Increases it","Increases airway resistance","Has no effect"],"e":["Wrong. Decreases.","Wrong. Opposite.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":2,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"Which describes the tendency of the lungs and chest wall at rest?","o":["Lungs tend to collapse inward and the chest wall to spring outward","Neither has recoil","Lungs expand outward and the chest wall collapses inward","Both tend to collapse inward","Both tend to expand outward"],"e":["Correct. Elastic recoil.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Opposite.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"683","k":"Lung and chest wall properties"},{"s":"How does hypoxia affect pulmonary vessels compared with systemic vessels?","o":["Constricts both","Has no effect on pulmonary vessels","Dilates pulmonary vessels and constricts systemic vessels","Constricts pulmonary vessels and dilates systemic vessels","Dilates both"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Opposite.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"684","k":"Pulmonary circulation"},{"s":"What is the purpose of hypoxic pulmonary vasoconstriction?","o":["To increase dead space","To lower pulmonary artery pressure","To increase cardiac output","To raise systemic blood pressure","To shift blood from poorly ventilated to well-ventilated regions"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Raises it.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"684","k":"Pulmonary circulation"},{"s":"Chronic hypoxic vasoconstriction can lead to which?","o":["Mitral regurgitation",