inds less CO2"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":2,"p":"684","k":"Pulmonary circulation"},{"s":"Pulmonary vascular resistance is calculated as which?","o":["(Aortic pressure − right atrial pressure) / cardiac output","Left atrial pressure / pulmonary artery pressure","Heart rate × stroke volume","(Pulmonary artery pressure − left atrial pressure) / cardiac output","Cardiac output × pulmonary artery pressure"],"e":["Wrong. Systemic.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Cardiac output.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"684","k":"Pulmonary circulation"}]},{"t":"V/Q mismatch, alveolar gas and hypoxemia","q":[{"s":"What is the V/Q ratio at the apex of the upright lung?","o":["0","3","1","Infinity","0.6"],"e":["Wrong. Shunt.","Correct. Wasted ventilation.","Wrong. Ideal.","Wrong. Dead space.","Wrong. Base."],"a":1,"p":"685","k":"Ventilation/perfusion mismatch"},{"s":"What is the V/Q ratio at the base of the upright lung?","o":["1","3","0","0.6","Infinity"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Apex.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct. Wasted perfusion.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"685","k":"Ventilation/perfusion mismatch"},{"s":"Which statement about ventilation and perfusion in the upright lung is correct?","o":["Both are greater at the base than at the apex","Both are greater at the apex","Ventilation is greater at the apex, perfusion at the base","Perfusion is greater at the apex","They are equal everywhere"],"e":["Correct.","Wrong. Opposite.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"685","k":"Ventilation/perfusion mismatch"},{"s":"Why does reactivated tuberculosis favor the lung apex?","o":["TB thrives in the higher oxygen tension of the apex","The apex has more lymphatics","The apex has more macrophages","The apex has more surfactant","The apex has more blood flow"],"e":["Correct. High V/Q.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not cor