rong. 2,3-BPG."],"a":2,"p":"686","k":"Carbon dioxide transport"},{"s":"In the lungs, oxygenation of hemoglobin promotes release of CO2 from red cells. What is this called?","o":["The Haldane effect","The chloride shift","The Bohr effect","Hysteresis","Hypoxic vasoconstriction"],"e":["Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. CO2 and H+ shift the ODC.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"686","k":"Carbon dioxide transport"},{"s":"As bicarbonate leaves the red cell in tissues, which ion enters in exchange?","o":["Hydrogen","Potassium","Chloride","Calcium","Sodium"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct. Chloride shift.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":2,"p":"686","k":"Carbon dioxide transport"},{"s":"CO2 binds to which part of deoxygenated hemoglobin to form carbaminohemoglobin?","o":["The porphyrin ring","The N-terminus of globin","The heme iron","The 2,3-BPG pocket","The C-terminus of globin"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":1,"p":"686","k":"Carbon dioxide transport"},{"s":"Normal adult hemoglobin is made of which subunits?","o":["2 α and 2 γ","4 β","2 α and 2 δ","2 α and 2 β","1 α and 1 β"],"e":["Wrong. Fetal.","Wrong. HbH-like.","Wrong. HbA2.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"687","k":"Hemoglobin"},{"s":"Why does the oxyhemoglobin dissociation curve have a sigmoidal shape?","o":["Myoglobin binds O2 first","2,3-BPG binds O2","CO2 competes with O2","Hemoglobin has one heme","Positive cooperativity among the four subunits"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Four.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"687","k":"Hemoglobin"},{"s":"Why is the myoglobin O2 binding curve not sigmoidal?","o":["Myoglobin is a monomer with one heme and shows no cooperativity","Myoglobin has four hemes","Myoglobin carries CO2","Myoglobin binds 2,3-BPG","Myoglobin has lower O2 affinity"],"e":["Correct.","Wrong. One.","Wro